  "caption": "Linux kernel hands attackers root through a page-cache bug no one was watching. CVE-2026-46331 (pedit COW) in act_pedit lets an unprivileged user corrupt the cached ELF of /bin/su and get a root shell on the next invocation. Public PoC exists. Affected: RHEL, Debian, Ubuntu 24.04. Fixed in v7.1-rc7. Patch now. Restrict unprivileged namespaces where possible. Monitor namespace creation and setuid execution. The page cache is shared memory. Treat it like it is.\n\nFollow for real kernel and AI security breakdowns without the fake panic.",
